# Find a navigation-safe approach pose near a registered scene object.
#
# Input: an object_id from scene's registry. Optionally a desired
# `clearance_m` (extra free-space margin around the result, in metres) and
# a max search radius `search_radius_m` (cap the BFS — beyond this we
# give up rather than find a useless faraway free cell).
#
# Output: a PoseStamped in the map frame whose `position.{x,y}` lies in a
# free cell of the latest occupancy_grid, at least `clearance_m` from any
# obstacle, and within `search_radius_m` of the object's centre. The
# `pose.orientation` faces back toward the object (yaw = atan2(obj-pose,
# pose-obj)) so the LLM doesn't have to compose facing logic. `reachable`
# is false when we couldn't satisfy the constraints — caller should treat
# that as "object is unreachable from the current map" and pick a
# different target. `reason` carries a short human-readable explanation
# either way.
std_msgs/String object_id
float32 clearance_m       # 0 → use service-side default (e.g. inscribed_radius + 0.1m)
float32 search_radius_m   # 0 → use service-side default (e.g. 3.0m)
---
bool reachable
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped pose
string reason
